course: dictionary
lesson: 14430
title: Breaking down a word: over-
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts, and the start of a word can change its meaning. «Over» at the start of overworking means too much. So overworking means working too much, more than is good for you.
explain: Look at the context: «Mia felt sick and dizzy because she had been overworking all month.» Sick and dizzy are signs of being tired and ill. Working too much made her ill, so overworking means working too hard or too long.
explain: Overworking can also be something one person does to another. «The cruel master was overworking his horses, and they could hardly stand.» The master is making the horses work too much, which is unkind. Ask yourself: who is working, and is it too much?
fact: Overworking means working too hard or too long.
fact: Overworking someone means making them work too much.
fact: «Over» at the start of a word often means too much, as in overeat, overflow and overwork.
fact: Overworking can be a noun, as in «Overworking can make people tired and ill.»
fact: Overworking can make people tired and ill, so rest matters.
exercise: «Dad was overworking at the factory all week.» What does overworking mean? | Sleeping in on a sunny day | Playing games with friends | Eating his lunch slowly | *Working too hard or too long
exercise: The word «overwork» starts with «over». What does «over» mean here? | Finished and done | *Too much | Happy and free | Under the table
exercise: «The cruel master was overworking his horses.» What is the master doing? | Feeding the horses a treat | *Making the horses work too much | Taking the horses to the park | Teaching the horses to swim
test: «Tired and ill, Mia said she had been overworking all month.» What does overworking mean? | Reading a long book | Resting in bed all day | Singing with friends | *Working too much or too long
test: Which word shows the same idea of «too much»? | Blue | *Overeating | Underwater | Teacher
exam: Why can overworking be bad for people? | *Because it can make them tired and ill | Because it makes them rich | Because it makes them taller | Because it makes them invisible
